<% content_for :title, "Privacy notice — WE Match" %>

<div class="card participant-card">
  <h1>WE Match privacy notice</h1>
  <p class="muted">How WE Match uses information you share when you join and take part.</p>

  <h2>What we collect</h2>
  <p>
    When you join or take part in WE Match we may collect your name, email address,
    time zone, group membership, the topics and time windows you choose, whether you
    were matched, and (after a conversation) your feedback answers.
  </p>

  <h2>How we use it</h2>
  <p>
    We use this information to run matching rounds: send invitations, introduce pairs
    who chose the same topic and window, and ask for short follow-up feedback. We may
    also look at anonymised totals (for example, which topics or focus areas came up
    most) so the WE Community can improve the programme.
  </p>

  <h2>Who can see what</h2>
  <ul>
    <li>Your match does <strong>not</strong> see your private feedback answers (including which subtopic resonated).</li>
    <li>Introduction emails show names, the shared topic, and the shared time window so you can contact each other.</li>
    <li>Women Emerging Community Managers can see participant details and responses inside WE Match so they can run and support the programme.</li>
  </ul>

  <h2>Emails</h2>
  <p>
    Joining a group means we may email you about WE Match for that group (invitations,
    reminders, introductions, and feedback requests).
  </p>

  <h2>Questions</h2>
  <p>
    If you have questions about this notice or your data, contact your Community Manager
    or Women Emerging.
  </p>

  <p class="muted">
    This notice is for WE Match participants. It may be updated as the programme develops.
  </p>
</div>
